  icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 9266273b8f123004195741f969177dda, type: 3}
  title: Features
  sections:
  - heading: What are they ?
    text: "Features are the main types that define the behaviours of any gameplay
      elements. Features are C# types that don't derive from MonoBehaviour, but that
      derive from Feature. They are meant to be lightweight, as independant as possible,
      and should work by composition (see \u2192 components)"
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Naming convention
    text: To tell them apart from components, which can sometimes have very similar
      names, you can prepend <b>F_</b> to your feature name.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  loadedLayout: 1
